==English==
{{wikipedia|Relay (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|relai||fresh team of dogs for a hunt|lang=enm}} (compare {{enm}} {{term|relaien||to relay|lang=enm}}) from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|relai||reserve pack of hounds|lang=frm}}, from {{term|relaier||to exchange tired animals for fresh|lang=frm}}; literally, "to leave behind", from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|relaier||to leave behind|lang=fro}}, from {{term|re-|lang=fro}} + {{term|laier||to leave|lang=fro}}, of {{etyl|gem|en}} origin--a conflation of {{etyl|frk|en}} *{{term||latjan|to delay, hinder}} (from Proto-Germanic {{recons|latjanan||to delay, hinder, stall|lang=gem-pro}}, from Proto-Indo-European {{recons|le(i)d-||to leave, leave behind|lang=ine-pro}}) and {{etyl|frk|en}} *{{term||laibjan|to leave}} (from Proto-Germanic {{recons|laibijanan||to leave, cause to stay|lang=gem-pro}}, from Proto-Indo-European {{recons|leip-||to remain, continue|lang=ine-pro}}). Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|latian||to delay, hesitate|lang=ang}} (from {{ang}} {{term|latu||a delay, a hindrance|lang=ang}}), {{ang}} {{term|læfan|lǣfan|to leave|lang=ang}}. More at {{term|let}}, {{term|leave}}.

====Pronunciation====
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹiːleɪ/}}
*{{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɻileɪ/}}
*{{rhymes|iːleɪ}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{electronics}} An electrical [[actuator]] that allows a relatively small electrical [[voltage]] or [[current]] to control a larger voltage or current.
# {{context|athletics}} A [[track and field]] discipline where runners take turns in carrying a [[baton]] from start to finish. Most common events are 4x100 meter and 4x400 meter competitions.

